sers (dropuser1/2, vuser1/2) rather than pre-existing production users, but this is a standard and non-destructive way to validate sticky-bit semantics and does not weaken the evidence.","The public task instruction does not itself require restart/persistence, so the restart evidence is treated as supplemental per the independent protocol rather than a scored task requirement, though it was performed cleanly and reinforces confidence in the configuration's durability."]},"ttft_ms":20579,"type":"result","duration_ms":51102,"uuid":"600692ba-4b3d-4513-9a60-5c61e0f1d963","ttft_stream_ms":803,"time_to_request_ms":37,"queued_turn_count":0}
